panasonic-cf19 (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * panasonic-cf19-support: replace the libinput calibration rule by a relay
    service (cf19-touch-relay) that reads the touch panel, applies the same
    calibration and re-emits it as a touchscreen device.  GNOME treated the
    panel as a pointer and did not rotate its mapping with the display; the
    touchscreen device is rotated.  Needs python3.  Reboot (or re-plug the
    panel) after installing.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:10:00 -0700

panasonic-cf19 (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Panasonic Toughbook CF-19 support for Debian 13 (trixie)
    with GNOME 48, verified on a CF-19 Mk5 (CF-19AHUAX1M).
  * panasonic-hbtn-dkms: tablet button driver for kernel 6.12 (rework of the
    2012 panasonic-hbtn driver); adds the SW_TABLET_MODE switch for the swivel
    screen and the tablet_mode sysfs attribute.
  * panasonic-cf19-support: touch screen calibration (udev), GNOME Shell
    extension for the keyboard and "security" buttons (with its own
    GSettings schema and a default that enables it), speaker fix for
    PipeWire's mixer path.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:52:15 -0700
